    <string name="hf_help_title">How to Play Hanafuda (Koi-Koi)</string>
    <string name="hf_help_text">Koi-Koi is played over several rounds, one per month. Capture cards to form combinations (yaku) and score the most points.\n\nEach turn, play one card from your hand. If a card of the same month is on the field, you capture both; if two match, you choose one; if none match, your card stays on the field. Then tap the deck to turn up its top card and match it the same way.\n\nThe cards have four classes: Brights, Animals, Ribbons and Plains. Combinations include three, four or five Brights, Boar-Deer-Butterflies, five Animals, red poetry or blue Ribbons, five Ribbons and ten Plains. The full set adds the viewing hands and red-and-blue Ribbons.\n\nWhen you make a new combination, choose: Koi-Koi to keep playing for more, or Shobu to score now and end the round. Seven points or more count double, and so do points won after the opponent called Koi-Koi. If the cards run out, the last player to call Koi-Koi keeps their points.\n\nUndo takes back a hand play until you turn up the deck.</string>
